    {
      "id": "ai-assist-author",
      "label": "AI-Assist Author",
      "note": "Held alongside one of the other writer roles, not instead of one, but a writer acts as exactly one role at a time. The aiAssist id in articleTypes is the article type, not this role — the two are deliberately spelled differently, and the aiAssist entries inside the access publish lists are that type."
    },
    {
      "id": "free-author",
      "label": "Free Author",
      "note": "The one writer role that exists in Sanity today. Its Free resource is unfiltered — Publish on _type == \"freeArticle\" — so it self-publishes every type, Duo and AI-Assist included, and already covers PubAll on its own. Duo self-publishing is a consequence of that grant, not an editorial rule: the target model keeps Duo out of every self-publish row."
